<http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/assertion> {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-wavelength> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-wavelength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Turing wavelength selection" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-wavelength> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The spacing of a Turing pattern at onset is set by the reaction rates and diffusivities, not by the size of the tissue, so changing these parameters predictably changes the number of repeated elements." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-wavelength> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/TestableHypothesis> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-wavelength> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "at onset k_c^2 = \\sqrt{\\det J/(D_u D_v)}, \\lambda_c = 2\\pi/k_c; under uniform rescaling of D, \\lambda \\propto \\sqrt{D}" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-wavelength> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Assumptions: near onset of instability, two species, domain large compared with the wavelength. Formal status: proved by linear analysis. Away from onset, the selected wavelength depends on nonlinear terms and history." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-wavelength> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/proposedTest> "Alter morphogen production, degradation or diffusion in a developing tissue (e.g. Hox dosage or Bmp/Wnt inhibition in mouse limb buds) and test whether digit or element number changes in the direction and proportion the dispersion relation predicts." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-wavelength> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hypothesisType> "model-theorem" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-wavelength> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "Alan Turing (1952) The chemical basis of morphogenesis" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-wavelength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1226804> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-wavelength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1252960> .
}
